{"text": "The Photos.\n\nMum looked at the photo carefully. Then she went out to the balcony.\n\n\"Come here,\" she said. \"Look at the beach. What can you see?\"\n\nMateo looked. He saw the sand, the black rocks, the café and many people.\n\n\"Everyone on that beach can see our house,\" said Mum. \"It's yellow, so it's very easy to see. This person doesn't know it's ours.\"\n\nMateo felt better. Mum was right.\n\n\"But now I want to know something,\" he said. \"Where does this person take the photos?\"\n\nMum smiled. \"Then find the answer. You have a lot of time.\"\n\nMateo looked at all the photos again, one by one.\n\nThey all showed the same beach, with the same black rocks. They were all from high up, too. The swimmers looked very small.\n\n\"The person is somewhere high,\" he told Mum. \"Higher than the café, but lower than our hill.\"\n\n\"A tree?\" asked Mum.\n\n\"There aren't any trees on the beach.\"\n\nMateo took his own photo from the balcony. Then he compared it with the stranger's photos. His photo was from the side. The stranger's photos were from the middle of the beach.\n\nHe found other small things, too. In one photo, there was a red float. In another photo, there was a wooden step in the corner.\n\nThen a new message came.\n\n\"A little boy was in the water today. He was afraid of the waves. I told him, 'Head up! Kick your legs!' He did very well.\"\n\nMateo read it again. Head up. Kick your legs.\n\nHe knew those words. But from where?\n\nIt was the last week of the summer holiday. The doctor was going to take off the cast on Friday.\n\nOn Thursday, the photo came at seven, as usual. But this time, it wasn't the sea.\n\nIt was an empty red chair, high above the sand. On the chair, there was an old red hat.\n\nUnder the photo, there was a short message. \"Tomorrow is my last day here. Thank you for watching the sea with me.\"\n\nThe cast was going to come off tomorrow. And tomorrow, he was going to find the stranger.", "textSha256": "cafd02b68e3